course: dictionary
lesson: 13737
title: The meaning of intention
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An intention is what you plan or mean to do. It is your aim or purpose. «Mia had the intention of tidying her room before tea.» Her plan was to tidy her room, so intention means plan or aim.
explain: Intention can also mean what you meant to happen. «Sam broke the vase by accident. He had no intention of breaking it.» The words «by accident» and «no intention» tell you Sam did not mean to break it. Judging intention helps us decide whether someone did something on purpose.
explain: Look for clue words such as plan, aim, meant, or on purpose. The phrase «have no intention of» means you do not plan to do something at all: «I have no intention of eating cold soup» means I will not eat it.
fact: An intention is what you plan or mean to do.
fact: «Good intentions» means you meant to do something kind or helpful, even if things did not turn out well.
fact: A «learning intention» is what a teacher says you will learn in a lesson.
fact: In church, an intention is a person or purpose that a prayer or Mass is offered for.
fact: The old-fashioned phrase «his intentions» can mean whether a man plans to marry someone.
exercise: «Mia had the intention of tidying her room before tea.» What does intention mean here? | A broken toy | A type of tea | A loud noise | *A plan or aim
exercise: «Sam broke the vase by accident. He had no intention of breaking it.» What does this show? | Sam broke it on purpose | *Sam did not mean to break it | Sam likes vases | Sam is very tall
exercise: A teacher writes a learning intention on the board. What is it? | A rule about noise | A picture of the playground | *What pupils will learn in the lesson | A list of who is absent
test: «She had good intentions, but her plan went wrong.» What does good intentions mean? | She had a lot of money to spend | *She meant to do something kind or helpful | She forgot her plan | She was very rich
test: Which phrase means you do not plan to do something at all? | good intentions | learning intention | in church | *have no intention of
exam: In ethics, why does it matter what someone's intention was? | To decide what colour to paint the room | *To judge whether they meant the harm | To count how many people were there | To find the date
